{
  "title": "AppFlowy \u2014 productivity (70,947\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: AppFlowy\nDomain: productivity | Scale: large | Stars: 70,947\nProblem: AppFlowy provides an open-source alternative to Notion that prioritizes data ownership, privacy, and mobile compatibility while offering collaborative workspace features for projects, wikis, documentation, and team management.\nTarget users: Teams and individuals seeking Notion alternatives, Organizations concerned with data privacy and control, Remote workers and collaborative teams, Knowledge workers managing projects, wikis, and documentation\nCore features: Database/Grid views for task and project management; Kanban board for task visualization; AI-powered workspace assistance; Sites/documentation publishing; Multi-device synchronization (desktop, mobile, web); Self-hosting capabilities; Template library; Real-time collaboration\nIntegrations: AI services, Cloud storage for self-hosting, App Store (iOS), Play Store (Android), FlatHub (Linux), Snapcraft (Linux)\nTech stack: Flutter (cross-platform: iOS, Android, macOS, Windows, Linux, Web) + Rust + Unknown (likely embedded or cloud-based) + Self-hostable with desktop/mobile distribution via multiple platforms\nKey libraries: Flutter, Rust, C++, CMake\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Cross-platform development using Flutter enables single codebase for desktop, mobile, and web while maintaining native performance.\n- Rust backend chosen for performance, memory safety, and reliability in core data synchronization and offline-first capabilities.\n- Self-hosting and data privacy are primary differentiators; architecture designed to support both cloud and on-premises deployment.\n- Emphasis on open-source (AGPL) and community contributions with clear contribution guidelines and public roadmap for transparency.",
